      "writtenOn": "2023-07-26T11:51:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. Thanks for the suggestion. I have re-implemented the communication protocol library with `serde` and (de)serialize the bytes in the host and rialto with `ciborium`.\n\nIt\u0027s true that in that sense the `ciborium_io`\u0027s `Read`\u0026`Write` can replace my own ByteChannel and I don\u0027t need to build another layer of `MessageChannel` on top of it.",
      "parentUuid": "41ef3403_c23be874",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 6,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "bc9a8646864e03d3500016348044aa0be5f9a386",
